{"name":"Gnocchi Beige","hex":"#ffeebb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gnocchi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Italian pasta-like dumpling(s) made of potato or semolina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gnocchi"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gnocchi","blocks":[{"text":"Gnocchi are a varied family of pasta-like dumplings in Italian cuisine. They are made of small rolls of dough, such as those composed of a simple combination of wheat flour, potato, egg, and salt. Variations of the dish supplement the simple recipe with flavour additives, such as semolina flour, cheese, breadcrumbs, cornmeal or similar ingredients, and possibly including herbs, vegetables, and other ingredients. Base ingredients may be substituted with alternatives, such as sweet potatoes for potatoes or rice flour for wheat flour. Such variations are often considered to be non-traditional."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Gnocchi_di_ricotta_burro_e_salvia.jpg/330px-Gnocchi_di_ricotta_burro_e_salvia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gnocchi","wikidata":"Q20063"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Gnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg/500px-Gnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Gnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg/1280px-Gnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Gnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg/500px-Gnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gnocchi in slowly simmered red sauce","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGnocchi_Red_Sauce.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Gnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg/500px-Gnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Gnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg/1280px-Gnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Gnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg/500px-Gnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gnocchi board or cavarola","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGnocchi_board_or_cavarola.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Creazione_gnocchi.jpg/500px-Creazione_gnocchi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Creazione_gnocchi.jpg/1280px-Creazione_gnocchi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_